        The bug was caused by an issue in the logging format used in the `Services.java` file, which may have led to incorrect or unclear log messages when Oozie services were being loaded or replaced. This could have resulted in difficulties in diagnosing the service startup process, ultimately causing the services to fail to start when logging was enabled.

